/-!
# Canonical-six H10--H14 frontier from an orthogonal finite-mode Schur problem

The H11 side is generated by one graph-norm estimate for the genuine smooth
core map into the minimal physical chart.  The H12 side now starts from one
finite physical mode subspace of the resulting common Hilbert space.

Orthogonal projection supplies the decomposition

`ℋ ≃L (Mode → ℝ) × Kᗮ`,

all four Schur blocks are extracted from the actual augmented Hessian, and
invertibility of the canonical `Kᗮ` block gives closed range and the exact
finite Schur kernel.  Hence neither a basis of the full kernel nor an arbitrary
full-space decomposition is a terminal input.
-/

namespace JanusFormal
namespace P0EFTJanusProgramPGlobalHessianCanonicalSixOrthogonalSchurFrontier4D

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option maxHeartbeats 10800000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 5400000

noncomputable section

